(4569207, 655884, 51793, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by walrus451:</b></div><hr/><i> I LOVE this image but I have one question:   why did you use such a small aperture and such a high ISO? </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Camera setting... I manually set the camera to ISO 100 but with one of the main settings it was set to ISO auto. I didn''t know it until after I got in the house and zoomed in that it was all noisy. As far as aperture, well I was shooting with a softbox and 2 strobes. The image was extremely bright and I needed to control it. A faster shutter speed wasn''t giving me what I wanted as the higher the aperture went the blurrier everything else got. So in shortness, it was an accident.</td>', 'Originally posted by walrus451: I LOVE this image but I have one question:   why did you use such a small aperture and such a high ISO?   Camera setting... I manually set the camera to ISO 100 but with one of the main settings it was set to ISO auto. I didn''t know it until after I got in the house and zoomed in that it was all noisy. As far as aperture, well I was shooting with a softbox and 2 strobes. The image was extremely bright and I needed to control it. A faster shutter speed wasn''t giving me what I wanted as the higher the aperture went the blurrier everything else got. So in shortness, it was an accident.', '2008-03-17 11:06:33.000000', NULL, 0),
(4569210, 655756, 47205, '<td valign="top">Congrats Sandy on the blue and a new personal best!!! God Bless</td>', 'Congrats Sandy on the blue and a new personal best!!! God Bless', '2008-03-17 11:12:48.000000', NULL, 0),
